      "message": "\u003e Something like \"Confirmed to work with NDK versions above 23.0.7599858\" would serve as a hint to guide people to a working version.\n\nBut that\u0027s just what works today - it would at least need a date of that confirmation. What if we instead say something like\n\n\u003e Certain build errors may be resolved by updating your NDK.\n\nI don\u0027t see much detail on your build error, so I don\u0027t know if we could make this more specific. But we could generally stick with the idea that you should try to update your tools?",
